  "provenance": {
    "kind": "original",
    "title": "La citadelle des deux presses",
    "description": "Original SS04 level combining Wizard exchange, fixed one-sided mirrors, stationary adjacent-attacking goblins, multi-crate lateral pressing and a chained water-platform press. Not a reproduction of a particular commercial room."
  },
  "necessity": {
    "mirrors": "Both mirrors are the only ray route between the starting island x1–5,y9–15 and the machine island x10–16,y1–7. Their individual wall ablations are exhaustively unsolvable.",
    "platform": "The exit island initially contains no actor; exchange cannot introduce the first actor onto it. Its sole walking entry is through (15,8), initially unsupported water. A submerged crate is therefore necessary.",
    "pistons": "A piston is necessary to create the water platform. The chosen witness uses the east-moving two-crate file and then the south-moving bridge press in a single cascade. The sentinel next to the bridge-trigger plate blocks direct Wizard occupation (verified fatal shortcut probe). Independent exhaustive necessity of each press was not run; no separate minimality claim is made.",
    "monster": "The starting island always contains two actors: it has no walking exit or piston, and exchanges preserve its actor count. Its original goblin starts away from the two exit-control plates. To leave both plates weighted after departure, this goblin must be moved onto a plate or exchanged out and replaced. Thus at least one monster exchange is necessary; neither final actor identity nor permanent survival of this specific goblin is claimed."
  },
  "validationNote": "64-direction successful authored witness, not a minimality claim. Full BFS reached its 350000-state cap; this is not an insolubility result. Mirror ablations exhausted their search spaces.",
